  <summary date="2026-09-09T17:10:26Z" status="Introduced in House">Litigation Transparency Act of 2025

This bill generally requires parties in a civil&#160;action&#160;to disclose to the court and other named parties the identity of any person (other than counsel) that has a right to receive a payment or thing of value contingent upon the outcome of the civil action. The bill also requires parties to produce the agreement creating the contingent right to payment or a thing of value.

These requirements apply to claims that are pending on or commenced after this bill's date of enactment.</summary>
